@startuml GitHub Actions CI/CD
' !theme plain

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center

actor "Developer" as Developer
participant "GitHub\nRepository" as GitHub
participant "GitHub Actions\nRunner\n(GitHub Hosted Ubuntu VM)" as Actions
database "Docker Hub\nRegistry" as DockerHub

Developer -> GitHub : 1. git push (e.g., to 'github-workflow')
activate GitHub

GitHub -> Actions : 2. Push event triggers\n.github/workflows/docker-build-push.yml
deactivate GitHub
activate Actions

Actions -> Actions : 3. Provision Runner &\nCheckout source code
note right of Actions
  Actions checks out the repository
  code into the runner workspace
end note

Actions -> DockerHub : 4. Authenticate (`docker/login-action`)\nusing Repository Secrets
activate DockerHub
DockerHub --> Actions : Login Succeeded
deactivate DockerHub

Actions -> Actions : 5. Build Docker Image (`docker/build-push-action`)
note right of Actions
  Executes `docker build` using the
  Dockerfile in the repository.
  Can handle multi-arch builds.
end note

Actions -> DockerHub : 6. Push Docker Image (`docker/build-push-action`)
activate DockerHub
note right of Actions
  Uploads image layers & 
  manifest over network
end note
DockerHub --> Actions : Image accepted
deactivate DockerHub

Actions --> Developer : 7. Marks Workflow Run as Success
deactivate Actions

@enduml
